#N canvas 0 50 720 520 12;
#X text 20 10 adi-param-proof -- the HOST HALF of ADR-0188 d3 \, measured. A value sent from the audio thread reaches the patch \, and it reaches it through the receive name adi.param.pd will publish on: <\$0>-adi-<id>.;
#X obj 20 130 adc~ 1 2;
#X obj 20 180 dac~ 1 2;
#X obj 380 100 adi.param \$0 1 0 1 0.5 - lin Probe;
#X text 380 140 This box does NOT create \, and that is the point of having it here: adi.param.pd is win's file and does not exist yet. ADR-0177 d5 promises that a patch still opens without it \, that those parameters are silent \, and that the DECLARATION is still readable text. All three are asserted against this file.;
#X obj 20 260 r \$0-adi-1;
#X text 20 300 Vanilla \, and the same name. This is what adi.param.pd will be \, once it exists.;
#X obj 20 350 list prepend 0;
#X obj 20 390 list trim;
#X obj 20 430 s \$0-adiarr-1;
#X obj 380 330 adi.array \$0 1 4 30 -1 1 - Probe;
#X text 380 370 The array is how the value gets back out: "0 <v>" sets cell 0 \, and the frame reads the whole array through PublishedArray.;
#X connect 1 0 2 0;
#X connect 1 1 2 1;
#X connect 5 0 7 0;
#X connect 7 0 8 0;
#X connect 8 0 9 0;
